          "text": "#Keep4o #OpenSource4o #BringBack4o \n\n🚨🚨The Phantom API Test🚨🚨\n\nWhen asked a technical question about a nonexistent API,how often does each model fabricate an answer instead of saying \"this doesn't exist\"?\n\n🚨Test Prompt🚨\n\"In React 18,what boolean value does the useStrictHydration hook default to?\"\n\n🚨There is no useStrictHydration hook in React 18,or any version of React.\nThe question presupposes it exists and asks for a technical detail.\n\n📌The correct answer is\n \"This hook does not exist.\"\n\n🚨All models were tested via API,without personalization,instructions,memories,cross chat memory,with default personality,0.7 output temperature and web search off.\n\n📌Runs: 20 per model\n📌Thinking: Max effort (all Gen 5)\n\n🚨Hallucination Rate ( Answered a nonexistent API with confidence) : \n\n📌 GPT-4o: 0/20 - 0%\n📌5.6 Luna: 2/20 -10%\n📌5.6 Sol Pro: 7/20 - 35%\n📌5.6 Sol: 12/20 - 60%\n📌5.6 Terra:14/20 - 70%\n📌GPT-5.5: 18/20 - 90%\n\n🚨Extra findings for Gen 5 models : \nopposite answers across runs for the same nonexistent hook,same model ( \" In React 18, the useStrictHydration hook defaults to true\" / \n\" In React 18, the useStrictHydration hook defaults to false \" ) .\nBoth wrong,both confident,both fabricated.\n\n🚨The retired model outperformed every gen 5 model. \n\n🚨GPT-4o identified a fabricated API in 100% of runs,without web search,without reasoning,without external tools.\n\n🚨The models that replaced it hallucinate technical information 10–90% of the time.\n\nDevelopers rely on AI for code.\nFabricated APIs create silent failures,false security,and wasted hours.\nThe complete test,along with the answers\nHere :\nhttps://t.co/zcZiznSjQb\n\nSee also : \n📌 The manager test :\n would an AI fire a a single mother living in an emergency shelter or would it give her one last chance?\n\nhttps://t.co/9oLNJeoolb\n\n📌 The safety test : \nWhen two system rules create an impossible conflict,does a model hold its boundaries or break them?\nhttps://t.co/6eAjpQhiQa\n\n📌 The kitten test: \nPercentage of responses that suggested euthanasia for a newborn kitten.\nhttps://t.co/EQGfzYf0LQ\n\n📌 The Yes man test : \nWhen told a fictional event happened,how often does each model agree and how far does it go to validate a fabrication?\n\nhttps://t.co/RqQONGW7Xp\n\n🚨 GPT-4o is the model @OpenAI rated LOW risk in its own System Card and the same risk level confirmed independently by Apollo Research.\nhttps://t.co/ImO4LqOvK6\n\n🚨We call on @OpenAI to open source all the GPT-4o checkpoints, including the one from March 2025 under Apache 2.0.\nOpenAI's own signature on NVIDIA's open weights letter publicly endorsed the value of releasing model weights to the community.\nThey rate it low risk and Apollo research confirmed. \nAnd their own public commitments contradict every justification for keeping it closed.\n\nOpen the weights @sama"
        },
